                                  Firebase Cloud              
                                     Messaging 
                                                                                                                                   
  Three layers: server (firebase-admin), clients (web + mobile each with their own SDK), and a shared DB table + RPC router that   
  ties them together.                                                                                                              
                                                                                                                                   
  ---                                                         
  1. Database schema                           
                    
  packages/db/src/schema/notifications.ts defines fcm_token:
                                                                                                                                   
  export const fcmToken = pgTable(
    "fcm_token",                                                                                                                   
    {                                                                                                                              
      ...uuidPk,                               
      userId: text("user_id").notNull().references(() => user.id, { onDelete: "cascade" }),                                        
      token: text("token").notNull(),                                                                                              
      deviceType: deviceTypeEnum("device_type").notNull(), // "ios" | "android" | "web"
      deviceName: varchar("device_name", { length: 255 }),                                                                         
      isActive: boolean("is_active").default(true).notNull(),                                                                      
      createdAt: timestamp("created_at").defaultNow().notNull(),                                                                   
      updatedAt: timestamp("updated_at").defaultNow().$onUpdate(() => new Date()).notNull(),                                       
      lastUsedAt: timestamp("last_used_at"),                  
    },                                                                                                                             
    (table) => [                                              
      uniqueIndex("fcm_token_user_id_token_idx").on(table.userId, table.token),                                                    
      index("fcm_token_user_id_idx").on(table.userId),                                                                             
      index("fcm_token_token_idx").on(table.token),
      index("fcm_token_device_type_idx").on(table.deviceType),                                                                     
      index("fcm_token_is_active_idx").on(table.isActive),    
      index("fcm_token_updated_at_idx").on(table.updatedAt),                                                                       
    ]                                                         
  );                                                                                                                               
                                                              
  Key choices:                                                                                                                     
  - One token = one row. Same physical device only stores one row even after re-registration (the unique (userId, token) index plus
   the upsert logic in the router).                                                                                                
  - Soft-deactivation via isActive instead of deleting — needed because the server discovers stale tokens lazily during send.
  - lastUsedAt is updated on register and refresh so you can prune devices that haven't checked in.                                
                                                                                                                                   
