  All of them are optional. The codebase silently no-ops if they are absent (isFirebaseConfigured() guards), so the app boots      
  without FCM in dev / CI.                                                                                                         
                                                                                                                                   
  Mobile uses no env keys for FCM — Firebase config is bundled into the native binary via google-services.json /                   
  GoogleService-Info.plist (managed by @react-native-firebase/app and Expo prebuild).
                                                                                                                                   
  ---                                                         
  3. Server: firebase-admin initialisation     
                                                                                                                                   
  packages/api/src/lib/firebase.ts:
                                                                                                                                   
  import admin from "firebase-admin";                         
  import { env } from "@mentor/env/server";    
                                                                                                                                   
  let initialized = false;
  let initFailed = false;                                                                                                          
                                                                                                                                   
  export function isFirebaseConfigured(): boolean {
    return Boolean(                                                                                                                
      env.FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID && env.FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL && env.FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY
    );                                                                                                                             
  }
                                                                                                                                   
  function initializeFirebase(): void {                                                                                            
    if (initialized || admin.apps.length > 0) { initialized = true; return; }
    if (initFailed || !isFirebaseConfigured()) return;                                                                             
    try {                                                                                                                          
      admin.initializeApp({                    
        credential: admin.credential.cert({                                                                                        
          projectId: env.FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID!,                
          clientEmail: env.FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL!,                                                                                 
          privateKey: env.FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY!.replace(/\\n/g, "\n"),
        }),                                                                                                                        
      });                                                     
      initialized = true;                                                                                                          
    } catch (error) {                                         
      initFailed = true;                                                                                                           
      console.error("[firebase] Failed to initialize Firebase Admin:", error);
    }                                                                                                                              
  }                                                           
                                               
  export function getMessaging(): admin.messaging.Messaging | null {                                                               
    if (!isFirebaseConfigured() || initFailed) return null;
    initializeFirebase();                                                                                                          
    if (!initialized) return null;                            
    return admin.messaging();                                                                                                      
  }                                                           
                                                                                                                                   
  Things that bite if you skip them:
  - privateKey.replace(/\\n/g, "\n") — env files store the key with literal \n. Without this replace the SDK fails with an opaque  
  PEM error.                                                                                                                       
  - The double-guard (admin.apps.length > 0) avoids "default app already exists" errors when bundlers double-evaluate the module
  (HMR, edge runtime).                                                                                                             
  - initFailed short-circuits future attempts so you don't log spam.                                                               
                                                                    
  Build: apps/api/tsdown.config.ts must externalize firebase-admin (it has native deps). Otherwise the bundle compiles fine but    
  blows up at runtime with Cannot find module './...'.                                                                             
                                                                                                                                   
  ---                                                                                                                              
  4. Server: send logic                                       
                                               
  packages/api/src/lib/push.ts exposes three exports:
                                                                                                                                   
  export type PushPayload = {
    title: string;                                                                                                                 
    body: string;                                             
    imageUrl?: string;                                                                                                             
    deepLink?: string;
    data?: Record<string, string>;                                                                                                 
  };                                                          
                                               
  export async function sendPushToUser(userId, payload, options?)   // single user                                                 
  export async function sendPushToUsers(userIds, payload, options?) // many users (batched)
                                                                                                                                   
  Key behaviours:                                             
                                                                                                                                   
  1. No-op when unconfigured — if (!isFirebaseConfigured()) return; first thing.                                                   
  2. Quiet hours — calls isInQuietHours(userId) from notification-preferences.ts (computes in user's timezone, handles overnight
  ranges like 22:00–08:00). Skipable with bypassQuietHours: true for security/urgent notifications.                                
  3. Frequency limits — 3 marketing/week and 10 transactional/day per user, counted from the notification audit table where
  sentViaPush=true.                                                                                                                
  4. Multi-device fan-out — fetches every active token row for the user(s) and uses messaging.sendEach(messages), so iOS + Android
  + web all get the same notification.                                                                                             
  5. Auto-cleanup of dead tokens — when FCM returns messaging/invalid-registration-token or
  messaging/registration-token-not-registered, the row is set to isActive=false:                                                   
  const tokensToDeactivate: string[] = [];                    
  response.responses.forEach((result, index) => {                                                                                  
    if (result.error && (result.error.code === "messaging/invalid-registration-token" ||                                           
        result.error.code === "messaging/registration-token-not-registered")) {                                                    
      tokensToDeactivate.push(tokens[index]!.id);                                                                                  
    }                                                                                                                              
  });                                                         
  6. Platform-specific message shape is set on every send — same payload, three sub-objects:                                       
  {                                                                                                                                
    token, notification: { title, body, imageUrl? },
    data: { ...payload.data, deepLink: payload.deepLink ?? "", timestamp: Date.now().toString() },                                 
    android: { priority: "high", notification: { channelId: "default", sound: "default" } },                                       
    apns:    { payload: { aps: { sound: "default", badge: 1 } } },                                                                 
  }                                                                                                                                
                                                                                                                                   
  ★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────                                                                                  
  Note data values are coerced to strings (FCM only allows string values in data). deepLink ?? "" is the safe default — clients
  ignore empty strings.                                                                                                            
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────           
                                                                                                                                   
  ---                                                         
  5. Server: localized push (optional layer)   
                                                                                                                                   
  packages/api/src/lib/push-localized.ts + push-templates.ts add a thin layer on top of sendPushToUser:
                                                                                                                                   
  export async function sendLocalizedPush<T extends PushTemplate>(
    userId: string,                                                                                                                
    type: T,                              // e.g. "qa_new_answer"
    templateData: PushTemplateMap[T],     // typed: { lessonTitle: string }                                                        
    options?: LocalizedPushOptions                                                                                                 
  ): Promise<void>                                                                                                                 
                                                                                                                                   
  It looks up user.languagePreference, renders PUSH_TEMPLATES[type][locale] (10 types × 4 locales), and delegates to               
  sendPushToUser. Used like:                   
                                                                                                                                   
  sendLocalizedPush(question.askerId, "qa_new_answer", { lessonTitle }, {
    deepLink: `/lessons/${lessonId}`,                                                                                              
  });
                                                                                                                                   
  If you don't need i18n, you can skip this file and call sendPushToUser directly.                                                 
                                               
