  7. Web client integration                                                                                                        
                                                              
  Three files per web app (mirrored across web-learner, web-mentor, web-admin):
                                                                                                                                   
  apps/web-learner/src/lib/firebase.ts (browser)                                                                                   
                                                                                                                                   
  - Lazy-inits firebase/app + firebase/messaging (only when configured).                                                           
  - requestNotificationPermission() calls Notification.requestPermission(), then getToken(messaging, { vapidKey }), then sends the
  token to client.fcmTokens.register({ token, deviceType: "web", deviceName: navigator.userAgent.slice(0, 100) }).                 
  - setupForegroundListener(callback) wraps onMessage() — used to show in-app toasts when a push arrives while the tab is open.
  - unregisterFcmToken(token) for sign-out.                                                                                        
                                                                                                                                   
  apps/web-learner/public/firebase-messaging-sw.js (service worker)                                                                
                                                                                                                                   
  - Cannot import process.env — service workers don't go through the bundler. Config is delivered at runtime via postMessage:      
  self.addEventListener("message", (event) => {               
    if (event.data?.type === "FIREBASE_CONFIG") {                                                                                  
      firebaseConfig = event.data.config;                                                                                          
      initFirebase();                          
    }                                                                                                                              
  });                                                         
  - Uses the compat Firebase SDK (firebase-app-compat.js / firebase-messaging-compat.js) loaded from gstatic.com because           
  tree-shaken modular imports don't run inside service workers.                                                                    
  - messaging.onBackgroundMessage shows a system notification.
  - A notificationclick handler reads event.notification.data.deepLink and either focuses an existing tab (posting a               
  NOTIFICATION_CLICK message) or opens a new window.                                                                               
                                                                                                                                   
  apps/web-learner/src/components/notification-setup.tsx                                                                           
                                                              
  React component mounted in the root layout. It:                                                                                  
  1. Registers /firebase-messaging-sw.js.                     
  2. postMessages the Firebase config to all worker states (installing, waiting, active, plus navigator.serviceWorker.ready.active 
  because active can be null on first install).                                                                                   
  3. If permission is already granted, silently calls requestNotificationPermission() to refresh the token.                        
  4. Sets up the foreground listener → shows a toast via sonner and tracks via @mentor/analytics.          
  5. Listens for NOTIFICATION_CLICK SW messages and navigates to the deep link — but only if it's a same-origin relative URL       
  (startsWith("/") && !startsWith("//")) to prevent open-redirect attacks.                                                         
                                                                                                                                   
  ★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────                                                                                  
  The two-step "register SW then postMessage config" dance is needed because the SW lives at a static URL                          
  (/firebase-messaging-sw.js) so it can't read your bundler env vars. Don't try to template the SW file at build time — Next.js    
  doesn't process public/.                     
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────                                                                                
                                                              
