  ---
  9. What's left out (worth knowing)

  - Stable tracking — notification audit table records every send (sentViaPush=true) which is what powers the rate-limit counters. If you copy push.ts you also need that
  table or you'll lose frequency limiting.
  - In-app notifications are a separate concern — notifications and admin-notifications routers manage in-DB notifications independently of FCM. Push is just the delivery 
  channel.                                                                                                                                                                 
  - Tests live at:
    - packages/api/src/lib/__tests__/push.test.ts                                                                                                                          
    - packages/api/src/routers/__tests__/fcm-token.test.ts    
  - Coverage threshold is 80% repo-wide, so if you copy these files into another monorepo with the same pre-push hook, copy the tests too.                                 
                                                                                                                                                                           
